| `launcher.spare.max_load_per_cpu` | number | `0.25` | a number above 0 and at most 64 | `scripts/launch.py` (`load_launcher_config`); `spare` | Sets the largest max(1-minute, 5-minute) load average per cpu at which this host counts as spare, so a script the farm did not start in time runs here limited. An unknown load is not spare. load_launcher_config checks the numeric range before math.isfinite, so an oversized integer is a named CONFIG refusal; booleans, non-finite floats and out-of-range numbers are refused. | the wait itself: `launcher.farm.wait_seconds` | always |
